			},
			"date": "2023-04-19T00:04:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I no good with words, but I've been using Lit for years and I have felt no lack. I'm probably not best for making comparisons though, because I've never used React or Vue or anything, but I cannot imagine what people are saying when they say frameworks \"make it easy\" because I have felt like I've been missing anything I needed over the years, and its much easier to upgrade an adopted library than figure how to move up a framework major version tho the last I used of those was angularjs</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
